"SSEQueue — bounded FIFO of pending SSE events for a single dashboard
 connection. Isolates slow consumers so one stalled browser tab cannot
 block the tick loop from serving every other subscriber. §4.11, D6.14.

 Capacity is fixed at 256 events. `enqueue:` returns false once the
 queue is full (or closed), at which point DashboardSSE drops the
 subscriber and closes the underlying HTTP connection. A dedicated
 [block] fork drainer per connection pulls events off the queue and
 invokes `conn send:event:` — so even if that call blocks on a slow
 client the tick loop is unaffected.

 Implementation: pre-allocated ring buffer. Both enqueue: and dequeue
 are O(1) with zero allocation on the hot path — the previous
 copyWith:/copyFrom: implementation allocated a fresh N-element array
 on every enqueue and every dequeue.

 This class is intentionally minimal: no internal signalling primitive
 (Maggie lacks Channel), so the drainer polls with a short sleep when
 the queue is empty. In practice the tick cadence (≈5s) dwarfs the
 poll interval (200ms) so latency is dominated by enqueue frequency."

SSEQueue subclass: Object
  instanceVars: buf cap head tail count closed droppedCount

  classMethod: new [
    ^super new init
  ]

  classMethod: new: capacity [
    ^super new initCap: capacity
  ]

  method: init [
    ^self initCap: 256
  ]

  method: initCap: capacity [
    cap := capacity.
    buf := Array new: cap.
    head := 0.
    tail := 0.
    count := 0.
    closed := false.
    droppedCount := 0.
    ^self
  ]

  method: size [
    ^count
  ]

  method: capacity [
    ^cap
  ]

  method: isEmpty [
    ^count = 0
  ]

  method: isFull [
    ^count >= cap
  ]

  method: isClosed [
    ^closed
  ]

  method: droppedCount [
    ^droppedCount
  ]

  method: close [
    "Mark the queue closed. Subsequent enqueues return false; the
     drainer loop observes closure and exits once empty."
    closed := true.
    ^self
  ]

  method: enqueue: event [
    "Append event to the tail of the ring buffer. Returns true on
     success, false if the queue is closed or at capacity. O(1), no
     allocation."
    closed ifTrue: [^false].
    count >= cap ifTrue: [
      droppedCount := droppedCount + 1.
      ^false
    ].
    buf at: tail put: event.
    tail := (tail + 1) \\ cap.
    count := count + 1.
    ^true
  ]

  method: dequeue [
    "Pop the head of the ring buffer, or nil if empty. O(1), no
     allocation. Nils out the vacated slot to avoid retaining
     references to delivered events."
    | item |
    count = 0 ifTrue: [^nil].
    item := buf at: head.
    buf at: head put: nil.
    head := (head + 1) \\ cap.
    count := count - 1.
    ^item
  ]
